  "id": "mind-wandering",
  "term": "mind wandering",
  "definition": "In this historical source, mind wandering means a temporary drifting or straying of thought seen during acute illness, especially fever. It refers to a mild delirious state in which attention to the present weakens and the person’s mind turns away from current surroundings.",
